{{!-- The auth Surface, whole: the centred column, and the one card the site's state allows.

	{{> "auth/shell" flow="signin" surface="sign-in" eyebrow=(t "Members") title=(t "Sign in") subhead=…}}
	{{> "auth/shell" flow="signup" surface="sign-up" … subheadWidth="max-w-[42ch]"}}

	flow           `signin` or `signup` — which form, and whether invite-only has a branch
	surface        the `data-surface` marker the harness reads
	eyebrow/title/subhead   the column's own heading block
	subheadWidth   the subhead's measure — 40ch on sign-in, 42ch on sign-up

THE STATE MATRIX IS HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE. Four site shapes reach these two Surfaces — a visitor
who is already a member, an invite-only publication, members off entirely, and open signup — and
each of them is reachable from a menu item a buyer left behind after changing a setting. Keeping
the branches in one partial is what stops the two templates drifting apart on the third one.

Static partial names, not `{{> (lookup . "card")}}`: gscan rejects the inline dynamic form
outright, because a missing partial throws a page error rather than degrading, and the block form
that avoids that reads worse than this `{{#match}}` does.

The page is a flex column — `<body>` already is, and these two Surfaces carry no foot — so this
main is the growing middle and the card stays optically centred on the tinted field whatever the
viewport height. That is also why the design draws no footer here: there is nothing to sit below a
column that is meant to be centred. --}}
<main
	id="auth"
	class="bg-page-field flex flex-auto items-center justify-center px-8 py-16"
	data-surface="{{surface}}">
	<div class="w-full max-w-[460px]">
		<div class="mb-7 text-center">
			<p class="font-meta text-meta text-accent tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">{{eyebrow}}</p>

			<h1
				id="auth-title"
				class="font-display tracking-display mt-3.5 text-[40px] leading-[1.08] font-medium">{{title}}</h1>

			<p
				class="text-small text-muted mx-auto mt-3 leading-[1.6] text-pretty {{#if subheadWidth}}{{subheadWidth}}{{else}}max-w-[40ch]{{/if}}">{{subhead}}</p>
		</div>

		<div class="border-border bg-surface rounded-md border p-9 shadow-md">
			{{#if @member}}
				{{#match flow "signup"}}
					{{> "auth/signed-in" cardTitle=(t "You are already a member")}}
				{{else}}
					{{> "auth/signed-in" cardTitle=(t "You are signed in")}}
				{{/match}}
			{{else}}
				{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
					{{#match flow "signup"}}
						{{#if @site.members_invite_only}}
							{{> "auth/closed"}}
						{{else}}
							{{> "auth/sign-up-form"}}
						{{/if}}
					{{else}}
						{{> "auth/sign-in-form"}}
					{{/match}}
				{{else}}
					{{> "auth/closed"}}
				{{/if}}
			{{/if}}
		</div>

		{{!-- The notes belong to a card that can act, so they follow the same guards. --}}
		{{#unless @member}}
			{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
				{{#match flow "signup"}}
					{{#unless @site.members_invite_only}}
						{{> "auth/sign-up-notes"}}
					{{/unless}}
				{{else}}
					{{> "auth/sign-in-notes"}}
				{{/match}}
			{{/if}}
		{{/unless}}
	</div>
</main>
